# Gitignored paths that `git-wt step copy-ignored` may copy into a new worktree.
#
# This is an ALLOWLIST: with --require-include, nothing is copied unless listed
# here. That is deliberate. A blanket copy of ignored files would take target/
# (which reached 129 GB on this machine) and samples/private/ (real PII, which
# the benchmark walk excludes unless --include-private is passed).
#
# What a worktree needs to run the OCR tests and benchmarks:
text-detection.rten
text-recognition.rten
samples/passports/*
samples/id_cards/
samples/driving_licenses/
samples/misc/

# Deliberately NOT listed, and why:
#   target/                 build cache, regenerable, was 129 GB
#   samples/private/        real PII; opt-in via --include-private only
#   samples/local/          local-only track, not part of the default walk
#   *.gguf                  Tier-2 LLM weights, only needed for the LLM path
#   intent/                 local strategic intent, deliberately not shared
#   artifacts/ out/ _site/  run output and scratch
